    "JurisdictionSpecifics": "North Carolina applies a modified comparative negligence rule. A plaintiff may recover damages only if the plaintiff's fault is 75% or less, and any award is reduced by the plaintiff's percentage of fault. Ordinary negligence requires proof that the defendant breached a duty of care, causing injury to the plaintiff.",
